.SH "\fR3\&.0\&.0\fP / 2019-08-08"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Add option to specify executable file name (\fR#999\fP)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
e\&.g\&. \fR\&.command('clone', 'clone description', { executableFile: 'myClone' })\fP
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
Change docs for \fR\&.command\fP to contrast action handler vs git-style executable\&. ([#938] \fR#990\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBreaking\fP Change TypeScript to use overloaded function for \fR\&.command\fP\&. ([#938] \fR#990\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Change to use straight quotes around strings in error messages (like 'this' instead of \fRthis') ([#915])\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRAdd TypeScript "reference types" for node ([#974])\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRAdd support for hyphen as an option argument in subcommands ([#697])\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRAdd support for a short option flag and its value to be concatenated for action handler subcommands ([#599])
.IP "  \(bu" 4
e\&.g\&. 
.PP
\fP-p 80\fR can also be supplied as \fP-p80\fR\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRAdd executable arguments to spawn in win32, for git-style executables ([#611])
.IP "  \(bu" 4
e\&.g\&. 
.PP
\fPnode --harmony myCommand\&.js clone\fR\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRAdd parent command as prefix of subcommand in help ([#980])\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRAdd optional custom description to \fP\&.version\fR ([#963])
.IP "  \(bu" 4
e\&.g\&. 
.PP
\fPprogram\&.version('0\&.0\&.1', '-v, --vers', 'output the current version')\fR\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRAdd \fP\&.helpOption(flags, description)\fR routine to customise help flags and description ([#963])
.IP "  \(bu" 4
e\&.g\&. 
.PP
\fP\&.helpOption('-e, --HELP', 'read more information')\fR\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRFix behavior of --no-* options ([#795])
.IP "  \(bu" 4
can now define both 
.PP
\fP--foo\fR and \fP--no-foo\fR
.IP "  \(bu" 4
**Breaking** custom event listeners: 
.PP
\fP--no-foo\fR on cli now emits \fPoption:no-foo\fR (previously \fPoption:foo\fR)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
**Breaking** default value: defining 
.PP
\fP--no-foo\fR after defining \fP--foo\fR leaves the default value unchanged (previously set it to false)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
allow boolean default value, such as from environment ([#987])
.PP
\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRIncrement inspector port for spawned subcommands ([#991])
.IP "  \(bu" 4
e\&.g\&. 
.PP
\fPnode --inspect myCommand\&.js clone`
.PP
.SS "Migration Tips"
The custom event for a negated option like \fR--no-foo\fP is \fRoption:no-foo\fP (previously \fRoption:foo\fP)\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
program
  \&.option('\-\-no\-foo')
  \&.on('option:no\-foo', () => {
    console\&.log('removing foo');
  });
.fi
.PP

.PP
When using TypeScript, adding a command does not allow an explicit \fRundefined\fP for an unwanted executable description (e\&.g for a command with an action handler)\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
program
  \&.command('action1', undefined, { noHelp: true }) // No longer valid
  \&.command('action2', { noHelp: true }) // Correct
.fi
.PP
